{% comment %}
  Negotiation widget mount point.

  Deliberately thin: brand colors/voice, trigger rules (always-on,
  dwell-time, exit-intent, revisit, cohort/email token), and the
  ladder-driven copy are ALL merchant-configured from this app's own
  embedded admin - not from Theme Editor block settings - per the brief's
  "zero code/theme changes required per merchant" rule for everything
  except placement. The widget script below fetches that config at
  runtime, scoped by shop domain.

  This is a regular app BLOCK (target: section), not an app embed: the
  merchant drags it into their product template wherever they want -
  right below the buy buttons, say - via Theme Editor's normal "Add
  block" flow. Was an app EMBED (target: body, auto-injected on every
  page, activated once under Theme Editor > App embeds) - changed because
  the widget only ever does anything on product pages anyway (see the
  pageType/productId guard in widget.tsx), so a global body-injected embed
  bought nothing except an unremovable fixed-position launcher that
  collided with whatever else a theme already had pinned to that corner
  (sticky add-to-cart bars, other apps' widgets, iOS's safe-area, etc.).
  A block placed explicitly by the merchant has no such collision, since
  its position in the page flow is exactly wherever they put it.

  enabled_on restricts this to the product template only - it would be a
  silent no-op anywhere else (per the same pageType guard), so there's no
  reason to let a merchant add it to a page it can't do anything on.

  block.shopify_attributes on the mount div isn't strictly required for
  the widget to function, but it's what lets the theme editor highlight/
  select this exact block when a merchant clicks it, standard practice
  for app blocks.
{% endcomment %}
<div
  id="scopegen-nego-widget"
  data-shop="{{ shop.permanent_domain }}"
  data-page-type="{{ request.page_type }}"
  {% if product %}data-product-id="gid://shopify/Product/{{ product.id }}"{% endif %}
  {% if product %}data-variant-id="gid://shopify/ProductVariant/{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"{% endif %}
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
></div>
<script src="{{ 'negotiation-widget.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Negotiation widget",
  "target": "section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
